  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Given the vectors $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(a,b).$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(a,b) & =\u2016a-b\u2016 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({a}_{1}-{b}_{1})^{2}+({a}_{2}-{b}_{2})^{2}+({a}_{3}-{b}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5-3)^{2}+(0-1)^{2}+(3-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
